{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661308,"nonce":"wNyjVu/1LyPoNUeOelabYrxXsiE=","title":"Replace process-lifetime pid lock with a short write lock","message":"Today `cache/repo_cache.go` takes a pid lock for the life of the process, so an open TUI/webui blocks every CLI call (and every agent). Target model: one store, many processes, lock-free readers, serialized writers, no daemon.\n\n- Writers take an flock-style lock only across: re-read entity -\u003e append ops -\u003e commit -\u003e cache-file write. Sub-second.\n- Readers never lock. Opening the cache never fails because someone else has it open.\n- Keep a stale-lock story (pid + liveness check already exists) for crashed writers.\n\nDecision recorded: no daemon. Agents fire many short CLI calls; those must be cheap and must not depend on a server being up. The GraphQL/webui server is just one more process on the same library.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661308,"nonce":"PD/apoIIvJapxKxQ4o/MjcfRXPc=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661308,"nonce":"GRT9wjzSa00/0eF5k6ukki0zWl4=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}